# Citation File Format: https://citation-file-format.github.io/
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ParticleTracker in your research, please cite this software."
type: software
title: "ParticleTracker (pt3d): 3D+t Particle Tracking Library"

authors:
  - family-names: "Fukushima"
    given-names: "Masato"
  - family-names: "Ideguchi"
    given-names: "Takuro"

version: "1.0.0"  # Keep in sync with the version being cited.
date-released: "2026-09-09"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Ideguchi-Lab/ParticleTracker"
url: "https://github.com/Ideguchi-Lab/ParticleTracker"
abstract: >-
  A Python library for 3D+t particle detection and tracking in microscopy data,
  with trackpy-based linking, diffusion analysis, and napari visualization.
keywords:
  - particle tracking
  - microscopy
  - anomalous diffusion
  - optical diffraction tomography

